        "title": "Add ESLint import ordering and VS Code settings",
        "summary": "Introduced .eslintrc.json with plugin:import/recommended and import/order rule enforcing grouped, alphabetized imports. Added .vscode/settings.json enabling formatOnSave and source.fixAll.eslint code action. Scope limited to repo configuration files. Uses @typescript-eslint/parser and typescript resolver.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T16:16:24.071Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When a developer who uses this project saves a file, Visual Studio Code will now automatically tidy up the order of its internal code references, keeping them grouped and alphabetized. This happens behind the scenes because the project added invisible configuration files that tell VS Code to run this cleanup every time a file is saved. Any developer on the team who edits code will see their files automatically stay organized without having to manually fix line ordering.",
