        "v": 5,
        "title": "trimMessagesToFitTokenLimit adds terminal output simplification",
        "summary": "trimMessagesToFitTokenLimit now simplifies terminal command outputs via simplifyTerminalCommandResults, keeping only the 5 most recent full outputs. Trimming targets 50% of MAX_MESSAGE_TOKENS to reserve space for new messages, replacing the previous full-limit fill. Updates backend/src/util/messages.ts and corresponding tests.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T16:16:27.644Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When the assistant reads back a long chat to fit it into its memory, it now trims the conversation more aggressively, keeping only the 5 most recent terminal command outputs in full and simplifying the rest, while also filling only half of the available memory space instead of all of it, leaving room for new messages. If you look at a trimmed conversation today, you’ll notice older terminal outputs are shortened and the overall message history is more compact. This affects the internal tool that prepares the assistant’s chat history before it responds, and it’s already live in the codebase.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "de09f954e56d",
        "at": "2026-09-17T21:16:47.355Z"
      },
      "structured": {
        "constants": [
          {
            "name": "MAX_MESSAGE_TOKENS",
            "from": "MAX_TOTAL_TOKENS - systemTokens",
            "to": "maxTotalTokens - systemTokens",
            "path": "backend/src/util/messages.ts"
          }
        ],
