        "v": 5,
        "title": "Add type assertions to messages test suite",
        "summary": "Added explicit `as any` type assertions to content array accesses in `backend/src/util/__tests__/messages.test.ts`. This resolves TypeScript strict-mode typing errors when accessing `.text` properties on union-typed message content blocks. The change is limited to test files and does not affect runtime behavior or production code.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T16:16:15.178Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The test checks that terminal output messages get simplified correctly. The test was failing to compile because the message content can come in different shapes, and the test code wasn't telling the system which shape to expect. Adding a small hint to the test code tells the system it can safely treat those message pieces as flexible, so the test now builds and runs. Nothing about how messages are simplified actually changed, and only developers running tests would notice.",
